% ============================================================================
% season-start-month-number.query.adj — worked recall over the season/calendar
% bridge library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what numbered month does
% this season start in?" — it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s
% the grounded rule and asks binding queries. The answer is DERIVED, joining
% a season fact to a calendar fact, so every answer carries BOTH citations in
% its `steps` trail.
%
% Placed at the stdlib PACKAGE ROOT (not beside `earth-science/season-start-
% month-number.adj`) — the same cross-directory-import sandboxing pattern
% `mathematics/word-problems.query.adj` already established: the library
% itself lives in `earth-science/` and reaches its calendar sibling via a
% relative `../calendar/months.adj` import, which only resolves if the
% CONSUMING entry program (this file) sits at or above the package root, so
% both `earth-science/` and `calendar/` fall inside the CLI's sandboxed
% import subtree.
%
% Run (from this directory, the package root, so the relative import
% resolves):
%     ../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli season-start-month-number.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "earth-science/season-start-month-number.adj"

? season_start_month_number(summer, $N)      % expect 6  (direct: which month number does summer start in?)
? season_start_month_number($S, 12)          % expect winter (reverse: which season starts in month 12?)
? season_start_month_number(monsoon, $N)     % expect abstain -- "monsoon" is not a tabled meteorological season
